From 2b714b6cb5e4ac7bd4566af22e3601948c750d69 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jeanluca <jeanlucafp@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 13:25:48 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] fix(tmserver): route "-" guild chat to the guild like the
 legacy server

The client sends guild chat as MSG_MessageWhisper with an empty MobName,
the text prefixed by "-" ("--" for the alliance) and Color 3
(TMFieldScene InsertInChatList). messageWhisper took it as a whisper to an
empty name and answered "not connected", so guild chat never reached
anyone.

Port the "Chat Guild" region of _MSG_MessageWhisper.cpp:1426-1468:
MobName becomes the speaker's name and Color becomes 3; every other
in-play member of the speaker's guild receives the line unless it turned
guildchat off; "--" also reaches the guild the speaker's guild is allied
to; a player without a guild gets _NN_Only_Guild_Member_Can. Color is
written at String[128], where the 7662 client reads it (the legacy
writes String[96] for its own 100-byte whisper struct). Port the
"guildchat" toggle of _MSG_MessageChat.cpp:140-150 with its message
panel, whose exact text the client matches to flip its guild button.
The chat_guild log line stays unmodeled; the text is never logged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
